The verdict is **FINDINGS**, not PASS, because several checks were not done. I saw no failed load and no console error.

- **Build and server:** Port 8000 had no listener, so I started `python3 -m http.server` from `dist/` and stopped it afterwards. `make -n` shows nothing to rebuild. The `web/` files match `dist/`, and the `doom.wasm` hash prefix is `7afb94fa1ec64b5c`, the one `coder.md` records as current.
- **Load:** I loaded `/?r=site8` in Playwright. All 6 assets returned 200 and there were 0 console errors.
- **Canvas:** It is 640x400, shown at 1152x720 (16:10). The frame counter went from 369 to 425 in 1 s.
- **Screenshot:** It shows in-game view with HUD and plausible colours. It was taken a few seconds after load, so it is the attract demo, not a title screen.
- **Findings:**
  - Minor: the AudioContext "not allowed to start" warning appears twice before a user gesture. That is expected under autoplay policy. The owner is coder_input_audio.
  - I did not capture the title screen on this build, so the attract-demo explanation from `coder.md` is not independently confirmed.
- **Not verified:** First-frame timing, a clean rebuild, other browsers, audio after a gesture, and warm-cache reload.

The report is `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.RLrOVV/report.md`. The screenshot, console log and server log are in the same directory.